{{also|kuken}}
==German==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|de|Kücken||Austria, alongside ''Küken''}}

===Etymology===
Via {{der|de|nds-de|-}} from {{der|de|gml|kuken}}, from {{der|de|osx|*kiukīn}}, from {{der|de|gmw-pro|*kiukīn|t=chicken}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|kuiken}}, {{cog|en|chicken}}. A related form is {{cog|gmh|kuchil}}, whence now obsolete {{m|de|Küchlein}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈkyːkən/|[ˈkyːkən]|[ˈkyːkŋ̩]}}
* {{audio|de|De-Küken.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|n}}

# [[chick]] {{gloss|young bird}}, [[fledgling]], [[hatchling]], [[squab]] (of a [[pigeon]] or [[dove]]))
# {{lb|de|figuratively}} the [[youngest]] in a group
# [[plug]] (as in a [[cask]])

====Synonyms====
* {{l|de|-baby}} ({{l|de|Elsterbaby}}, {{l|de|Eulenbaby}}, {{l|de|Taubenbaby}})
* {{l|de|junger}} {{l|de|Vogel}}
* {{l|de|-junges}} ({{l|de|Adlerjunges}}, {{l|de|Amseljunges}}, {{l|de|Kormoranjunges}})
* {{l|de|Jungvogel}}
* {{l|de|Nestjunges}}
* {{l|de|Nestling}} ({{l|de|Adlernestling}}, {{l|de|Falkennestling}}, {{l|de|Taubennestling}})
* {{l|de|Schlüpfling}}
* {{l|de|Vogeljunges}}
* {{l|de|Singerl}} (regional for a young hen or rooster, maybe derived from [[singen]])

